    feat(freshness-system): ship v1 context freshness hooks
    
    Adds seven active hook scripts that protect against stale-fact-reuse — citing
    file:line numbers, IPs, hostnames, or other source-tied facts from working
    memory after the underlying file has been modified.
    
    Components
    - 6 freshness handlers in src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/:
      freshness-session-start, freshness-user-prompt, freshness-pre-edit (the gate),
      freshness-post-read, freshness-subagent-start, freshness-subagent-stop.
    - install_hooks.py: atomic additive merge into ~/.claude/settings.json with
      backups before any write, malformed-target refusal, and matcher-collision
      detection that preserves existing user hooks.
    - Context freshness discipline section appended to src/superclaude/core/CLAUDE.md
      (auto-distributed via existing install_core_files).
    - Makefile sync-dev now also syncs hooks scripts into .claude/hooks/.
    - Wired into superclaude install orchestrator (step 5 after skills).
    - session-init.sh registration rewritten from fragile relative form
      ./scripts/session-init.sh to ~/.claude/hooks/session-init.sh.
    
    Tests
    - 13 pytest cases for install_hooks (atomic merge, malformed-target refusal,
      permission denied, backup-before-write, collision detection, etc.). All green.
    - freshness-test-suite.sh — 15 unit-test scenarios of the hook script logic
      (no API calls).
    - freshness-realworld-test.sh — 5 real-world scenarios via `claude -p` that
      validate Claude Code actually fires the hooks and recovers from blocks.
    - Live install verified on this machine via T05.01 (Phase 5 gating checkpoint).
    - Gate organically caught Write attempts during this session's own work
      (factual stderr, exit 2, telemetry row at ~/.claude/logs/freshness-hook.jsonl).
    
    Known v1 limitation
    The FileChanged registration was removed after live probing (T02.05) revealed
    Claude Code's matcher only accepts |-separated literal filenames, not regex —
    the design's matcher ".*" silently watched nothing. The freshness-file-changed.sh
    script stays in src/ as a v1.5 starting point. See CHANGELOG "v1.5 work items"
    for the FileChanged redesign options (static per-project watch list vs dynamic
    watchPaths from PostToolUse), Write-to-new-file refinement, install_hooks
    --no-orphans flag, reads.jsonl rotation, and session_id sanitization.
    
    Documentation
    - README highlights bullet pointing to docs/user-guide/freshness-hooks.md.
    - CHANGELOG.md with [Unreleased] Added/Fixed/Known-limitation/v1.5-work-items.
    - KNOWLEDGE.md with F1-F5 reusable debugging insights (FileChanged matcher
      semantics; grep -c double-count; flock -w timeout fallthrough; counter
      read-outside-lock race; per-session reads.jsonl semantics).
    - Full tasklist artifacts and 5 checkpoint reports at
      .dev/releases/current/freshness-system/ (20 deliverables, probe-finding,
      runbooks for the remaining interactive Phase 5 work).
    
